WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:04.430
Hey youtubers it’s charlie and since we’re
starting to learn more about the flash tv

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:09.530
series I thought it would be fun to talk about
some of the best flash comic book stories

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:10.890
they could use on the show.

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:16.200
Just to be clear season 1 just like Arrow
will be all about the origin story.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.140
Barry Allen will be learning about his powers
trying to solve his mother’s murder and

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.509
once we get to season 2 it will be about learning
the higher purpose.

00:00:24.509 --> 00:00:28.279
I feel like a lot of super heroes are selfish
with their powers right after they get them,

00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:32.009
at least until they get the Stan Lee speech,
with great power comes great responsibility.

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:35.940
Yes this is DC and that was Marvel, but every
super hero gets a version of that speech at

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.260
some point in their genesis.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.560
Wouldn’t it be great if it turned out that
John Wesley Shipp was the one to give Grant

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.140
Gustin the Uncle Ben speech?

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.100
Even if it turns out he’s not Jay Garrick.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.269
Real quick before we get started, if you didn’t
see yesterday I said I’d be doing Marvel

00:00:47.269 --> 00:00:48.570
movie videos every Tuesday from now on.

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.339
But if there’s really interesting DC stuff
to talk about I’ll do it then too.

00:00:51.339 --> 00:00:54.000
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.860
So let’s get started, here are my top 5
Flash stories.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:59.039
Number 5 - The Blitz Storyline.

00:00:59.039 --> 00:01:03.079
This like most of the good flash stories in
recent memory is Geoff Johns re-writing the

00:01:03.079 --> 00:01:04.780
origin of Professor Zoom.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.250
Or just Zoom in his pre-New 52 incarnation.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:11.320
What’s really cool about the story is that
Johns makes Wally West, the current Flash

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:14.180
at the time, complicit in the origin of his
greatest nemesis.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:19.250
And he ties it all back to the trial of Barry
Allen from the 1980s comics when he killed

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:20.250
the second Professor Zoom.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:24.720
This version of the Zoom character is Hunter
Zolomon the third version of the character.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:30.970
In the tv series it’s going to be Edward
Thawne, a riff on the second Professor Zoom

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:32.659
Eobard Thawne.

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:36.490
Number 4 - The Return of Barry Allen.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:40.700
This story happened in the same year that
they killed Superman in Death of Superman

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:44.030
and Bane broke Batman’s spine in Knightfall.

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:46.340
So bringing Barry Allen back from the dead
almost went unnoticed.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:47.340
It was a huge deal though.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.780
The character had been killed during Crisis
on Infinite Earths and was out of the comics

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:52.990
for about 7 years.

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:56.890
The story is all about Barry Allen rediscovering
himself and Wally West who had become the

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:59.190
new Flash, learning to share the spotlight.

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:02.690
This is a really good comic to read if you
want to learn about the physics of the Speedforce.

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:04.980
It’s a little like Mythbusters Flash Edition.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.770
It’s also got this crazy twist ending that’s
really awesome.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.950
Number 3 - Rogues Revenge.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:16.700
This is an awesome Flash story that focuses
on the Rogues during the events of Final Crisis.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:21.310
It picks up right after they kill Bart Allen
and gives you a really deep cut of what it’s

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:22.310
like to be a Flash villain.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:25.980
They’re a lot like the Suicide Squad in
that they’re not crazy evil like Zoom, but

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:27.310
they’re not good people either.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:31.170
It’s totally possible that they could do
a story like this in one or two episodes.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:35.190
Minus all the details of Final Crisis, just
a villain centric arc for an entire episode.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:39.850
It would be like Arrow just doing an episode
that mostly followed Slade instead of Oliver.

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:42.920
Number 2 - Flashpoint.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:47.500
This was the last Flash title that Geoff Johns
wrote and the last Flash book before the New

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.810
52 reboot.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:52.880
The story can be hard to follow if you’re
new to the idea of how time paradox’s work,

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:57.320
but essentially Zoom changes the past creating
a new timeline and Barry Allen fixes it but

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:01.720
in the process makes himself a living paradox,
essentially erasing himself from existence.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:05.740
But the solution to the problem is really
ingenious because they use it to explain how

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:11.390
in real life the DC, Vertigo and Wildstorm
comic book universes now exist together in

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:12.790
the New 52 reboot.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:17.420
So it solved this meta problem that dc comics
had with all their imprints and characters

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.390
existing separately and now they’re all
part of one big shared universe, just like

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:21.253
all the marvel characters exist in the same
universe.

00:03:21.253 --> 00:03:24.820
and my Number 1 Flash Story - Rebirth.

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:25.850
Rewind to the beginning.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:30.150
This story was actually the start of Geoff
Johns second run on The Flash with Ethan Van

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:31.150
Sciver.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:35.290
They had just rebooted Green Lantern and done
the Sinestro Core War, which by the way is

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:36.290
amazing.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:39.950
The story is all about the second return of
Barry Allen after the events of Final Crisis

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:44.099
and includes characters from all over The
Flash’s 70 year comic book history.

00:03:44.099 --> 00:03:48.040
It also treats the different types of powers
each version of The Flash had in interesting

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.040
ways.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.770
For instance, Jay Garrick’s super speed
is different from the way Barry Allen and

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.940
Wally West are affected by the Speed Force.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:58.400
So Rebirth reimagines the shared Flash Universe,
but remember this was from 2009, so since

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.610
then the Flash has been rebooted again for
the New 52 universe.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:06.410
Personally though these 5 stories are what
I consider to be the best, and just as a rule

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:09.520
of thumb you can’t go wrong with stories
written by Geoff Johns.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.080
He’s doing Justice League right now.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:15.480
So now it’s your turn, let me know what
your favorite Flash story is and let me know

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.840
if you think they’ll do a lot of comic book
story-based episodes during season 1 of the

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:21.469
show or if they’ll try to change a lot of
things.

00:04:21.469 --> 00:04:24.659
Like I said earlier, I’ll be doing Marvel
Universe videos every tuesday from now on

00:04:24.659 --> 00:04:26.129
unless there’s epic Superman Batman news.

00:04:26.129 --> 00:04:27.199
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:28.199
I’m still reserving Wednesdays for Arrow
and Flash whatnot.

